{"title":"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 10","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two six-sided dice are fair in the sense that each face is equally likely to turn up. However, one of the dice has the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> replaced by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the other die has the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> replaced by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> . When these dice are rolled, what is the probability that the sum is an odd number?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/4/164ba181fe102bfcab0d4f462a43d01ce757f128.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac{4}{9}\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac{5}{9}\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac{11}{18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"376\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On the first die, the chance of an odd number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/2/dd247efdc605218cc499decb7fc82e435f0a02e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{6} = \\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"49\" height=\"37\" />, and the chance of an even number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>On the second die, the chance of an odd number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/1/4e1965f8d70832ded66434c75a7bd52b75090af0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />, and the chance of an even number is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/4/7547747b133453d3c209cff6cfbf129aa67a6947.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>To get an odd sum, we need exactly one even and one odd.\n</p><p>The odds of the first die being even and the second die being odd is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/d/8fd779b2840d6fd09ce9925e625a90f160922d92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{1}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"75\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>The odds of the first die being odd and the second die being even is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/c/25c8e0a9f18c28faa70b905fc8184bbb3c3d3e47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3} = \\frac{4}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"75\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>The overall probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/d/28d807c6e70fc8934c610d76f2049736f89a1ad9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{9} + \\frac{4}{9} = \\frac{5}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"84\" height=\"37\" />, and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/b/55bdade53f471aab49f63d1a734979cc0c636640.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{D}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"29\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME\" title=\"1997 AHSME\">1997 AHSME</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1997 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1997\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1997_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1997 AHSME Problems/Prob